{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3060","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3060","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3060\",\"parent_revision\":\"a2fa209e484b1ac1dbaad9d9ff57231747be7658\",\"root_revision\":\"13acbe51317903b175f86c4359bb9e4ebe2a3aeda819ffd6d3f1a5f01d1b5f8a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe runtime strings that tell an agent what to call next steer it away from paginated navigation. The compact response's hint recommends loading full content as its first suggestion. The over-budget response tells a caller to request sections individually \u2014 advice a caller who already narrowed to one oversized section has exhausted. Neither mentions the paginated navigation parameters.\\n\\nAgents follow these strings. Documentation is a weaker lever: these are read on every call, at the moment of the decision.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:17:51.600851Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM: `_build_compact_manifest()` builds an `_hint` field whose first line is `Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)`, i.e. an unqualified full-content load is the first suggestion.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2306-2309\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      \\\"_hint\\\": (\\n          f\\\"Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"Load specific sections: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='<index, title, or /regex/>')\\\"\\n      ),\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Consumption contract R7 requirement (docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164)\\n  - Finding: R7 states \\\"A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\" \u2014 this _hint violates that by recommending `summary=False` (full content) before any narrowed option.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The _hint field's first line unconditionally recommends a full-content retrieval with no parameter, violating R7's first prohibition.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2306-2309 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `_build_over_budget_view()` unconditionally says to use `sections_index` and request sections individually \u2014 with no branch for a caller who already narrowed to one section via `section=`/`sections=` and got an over-budget response anyway.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2379-2387\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      \\\"_usage\\\": (\\n          f\\\"This response exceeded the {_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET}-token budget \\\"\\n          f\\\"({full_chars} chars in full form). \\\"\\n          \\\"Use the sections_index below to identify which sections you need, \\\"\\n          \\\"then request them individually:\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, sections=['Section Name'])\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='0,1,3')\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='/regex/')\\\"\\n      ),\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Same file, same function definition (no if/elif branches in function body)\\n  - Finding: The _usage string is built unconditionally with no conditional branching based on whether the caller already passed section= or sections= parameters. The function has no access to the original request parameters to make such a check.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The _usage text is a static template built without examining whether the caller already narrowed scope, thus recommends sectioning to a caller who may have already exhausted that option, violating R7's second prohibition.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2352-2392 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py` already builds a `next_call` hint of the form `backlog_view(selector=\\\"...\\\", navigate=\\\"...\\\", head=..., skip_tokens=...)` for EXTRACT-mode pagination \u2014 i.e. this paginated-navigation mechanism already exists in the package but is not mentioned by either hint in claims 1-2.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:487-490\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      next_call = (\\n          f'backlog_view(selector=\\\"{selector}\\\", navigate=\\\"{ordinal}\\\", '\\n          f\\\"head={head_tokens}, skip_tokens={next_skip})\\\"\\n      )\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: MCP Progressive-Disclosure Contract (docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md) documenting EXTRACT-mode parameters\\n  - Finding: The existing next_call mechanism already implements the R7-compliant hint format for token-bounded pagination, demonstrating that the capability exists but is not referenced by the over-budget and compact-manifest hints.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Disclosure handler already constructs next_call hints in the required format for EXTRACT pagination, but this mechanism is absent from the runtime hints in claims 1-2, making those hints R7-noncompliant (they never name a mechanism present in the response).\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:440-500 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` contains an \\\"R7 \u2014 Hints must be actionable\\\" requirement reading: \\\"A response that withholds content states what the caller must do to obtain it, using addresses valid in that same response. A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion, never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted, and never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies.\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      ### R7 \u2014 Hints must be actionable\\n      \\n      A response that withholds content states what the caller must do to obtain it, using\\n      addresses valid in that same response. A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as\\n      its first suggestion, never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted, and never\\n      name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: CONTEXT.md and MCP Progressive-Disclosure Contract (same document set)\\n  - Finding: R7 is the primary normative requirement governing hint construction across the entire backlog markdown consumption system.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The requirement is present in the contract with the exact wording stated in the claim.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: The item's Research section claims `_build_over_budget_view()`'s `_usage` \\\"appears already R7-compliant on direct reading (scoped-only options)\\\" per a note from a parallel impact-analyst run \u2014 this conflicts with claim 2 above (which asserts it unconditionally recommends sections without branching for narrowed callers). Resolve this conflict by reading the actual current `_usage` string yourself and reporting which claim is correct, with the exact current string quoted as evidence.\\nVERDICT: CONFLICT RESOLVED \u2014 CLAIM 2 IS CORRECT; ITEM ASSESSMENT WAS INCOMPLETE\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2379-2387 (same as Claim 2 evidence)\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Current _usage string (verbatim): |\\n      \\\"This response exceeded the 4000-token budget ({full_chars} chars in full form). Use the sections_index below to identify which sections you need, then request them individually:\\\\n  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, sections=['Section Name'])\\\\n  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='0,1,3')\\\\n  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='/regex/')\\\"\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Item's Code \u2014 Producers section (backlog item #3060 Research/Analysis)\\n  - Finding: Item contains TWO conflicting assessments: (1) first entry says \\\"appears already R7-compliant on direct reading (scoped-only options)\\\" and (2) second entry identifies the same function as violating R7 because \\\"When the caller already narrowed to `section=`/`sections=` and the *narrowed* slice itself is still over budget...this advice recommends an action the caller has already exhausted.\\\"\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Both assessments are now visible in the current item. The first assessment (\\\"appears R7-compliant\\\") is incomplete \u2014 it correctly observes that the _usage only offers scoped options, but misses that the function has no access to request parameters and thus cannot branch to offer different advice when the caller already narrowed. The second assessment correctly identifies the violation: the _usage is unconditional and will recommend sectioning even to a caller who already used section=/sections=. Direct code inspection confirms the second assessment is correct \u2014 the function receives no parameters indicating the caller's prior narrowing, and the _usage string is built without any branching. VERDICT: Claim 2 is correct; the first (\\\"R7-compliant\\\") assessment was incorrect.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2352-2392, backlog issue #3060 Research/Code\u2014Producers sections (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nSUMMARY OF VERDICTS:\\n\u2713 Claim 1 (VERIFIED) \u2014 _build_compact_manifest() violates R7 by recommending full-content load first\\n\u2713 Claim 2 (VERIFIED) \u2014 _build_over_budget_view() violates R7 by unconditionally recommending sections without branch for narrowed callers\\n\u2713 Claim 3 (VERIFIED) \u2014 disclosure_handler.py already implements next_call hints for EXTRACT-mode pagination\\n\u2713 Claim 4 (VERIFIED) \u2014 Consumption contract R7 requirement is as stated\\n\u2713 Claim 5 (CONFLICT RESOLVED) \u2014 Item contained two conflicting assessments; direct reading confirms Claim 2 is correct and the \\\"appears R7-compliant\\\" assessment was incomplete.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T10:00:13.371891Z</sub>\\n\\n## Fact-check verification \u2014 2026-09-19\\n\\nAll claims verified against origin/main (HEAD a75f11f0a5892979c5d72c316a6d3fe5a1007938, verified equal to origin/main via git rev-parse at verification time).\\n\\n### Claim 1: The compact response's `_hint` recommends loading full content as its first suggestion.\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2101-2104` (origin/main)\\n\\nThe code shows first line: `f\\\"Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)\\\\n\\\"` followed by the section-narrowing line. The first suggestion IS full-content load.\\n\\n### Claim 2: The over-budget response's `_usage` tells a caller to request sections individually, including when the caller already narrowed to one oversized section.\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2147 (function def), 2176-2184 (_usage field)` (origin/main)\\n\\nThe function `_build_over_budget_view(result, full_chars, selector)` receives no parameter carrying \\\"caller already narrowed\\\" state. The `_usage` field is built unconditionally and contains section-narrowing examples in all cases.\\n\\n### Claim 3: Neither `_hint` nor `_usage` mentions the paginated navigation parameters (`map=`, `navigate=`, `head=`, `skip_tokens=`).\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2101-2104 (_hint) and 2176-2184 (_usage)` (origin/main)\\n\\nDirect inspection and grep confirm: the strings `map=`, `navigate=`, `head=`, `skip_tokens=` do not appear in either field on origin/main.\\n\\n### Claim 4: The earlier grooming's premise that `map=True` output \\\"is documented as always under 2,000 tokens\\\" is false: MAP has no size bound.\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:1278-1286` (origin/main)\\n\\nQuote: \\\"`MapResponse.map_text` contains every formatted entry returned by `build_map()`. It is not bounded or paginated and does not omit entries.\\\" Explicit statement that MAP has no size bound, contradicting the \\\"always under 2,000 tokens\\\" premise.\\n\\n### Claim 5: No field of the over-budget response carries an ordinal that `navigate=` resolves.\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2068-2112 (_build_compact_manifest/_sections_index_from_result)` and `plugins/development-harness/docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md:29-36` (origin/main)\\n\\nThe over-budget response's `sections_index` field emits bracket-numbered indices like `\\\"[0] Name (count)\\\"` \u2014 the legacy scheme. Navigate's ordinal grammar is dot-path: `^\\\\\\\\d+(\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)*(\\\\\\\\.code\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)?$`. These are two different addressing schemes; no over-budget response field gives a resolvable dot-path ordinal.\\n\\n### Claim 6: The `backlog_view` `summary` parameter description lists loading full content before loading specific sections.\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2264-2274 (summary parameter Field description)` (origin/main)\\n\\nThe description text reads: \\\"_hint showing how to load full content or specific sections.\\\" The phrase lists \\\"full content\\\" before \\\"specific sections\\\" in textual order.\\n\\n### Claim 7: Plan Pe6bcc5c2 reports 100% complete, and none of its implementation is on origin/main.\\n\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n\\nSOURCE: Plan Pe6bcc5c2 (read via sam_plan, action='read') and #3060 owner comment (gh issue view 3060 --json comments, Jamie-BitFlight, 2026-09-19T06:59:44Z)\\n\\nThe plan has 3 tasks all with status \\\"complete\\\" (100% complete). Verification of implementation on origin/main: the plan's T1 task requires reordering the _hint to place \\\"Load specific sections\\\" FIRST. On origin/main, \\\"Load full content\\\" remains FIRST, proving the plan's implementation never shipped to main. The owner's 2026-09-19 comment on #3060 confirms: \\\"Plan `Pe6bcc5c2` reports 100% complete but its implementation was never merged (lived only on unpushed local branch `worktree-agent-a07620dae7e4b301c`).\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T10:26:10.746520Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM 8: Open PR #3642 (branch fix/3060-backlog-view-r7-hints) changes the \\\"remaining ownership\\\" (debt) table in plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md so that #3060 no longer appears in it, while #3060 stays open. Name the commit that makes the change.\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: gh pr view 3642 --json commits (2026-09-19)\\n  - Content: PR diff shows #3060 removed from debt table at ARCHITECTURE.md:1223\\n  - Commit: 7c9203b058334399810f16a1d005842222ce5f8e (message: \\\"docs(dh): drop #3060 from the progressive-disclosure debt table\\\")\\n  - #3060 state: OPEN (verified via gh issue view 3060)\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The commit 7c9203b058334399810f16a1d005842222ce5f8e removes #3060 from the \\\"Consumer guidance and contract identity\\\" row in the architecture debt table, while #3060 remains open, exactly as claimed.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 9: Exactly five agent files under plugins/development-harness/agents/ call `backlog_view(summary=False)` directly: alignment-analyst, backlog-item-groomer, classifier, impact-analyst, rtica-assessor. Report any other file under plugins/development-harness/ (agents, skills) that does so.\\n\\nVERDICT: REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: find plugins/development-harness/agents plugins/development-harness/skills -type f -name \\\"*.md\\\" (2026-09-19)\\n  - Agents confirmed: alignment-analyst.md, backlog-item-groomer.md, classifier.md, impact-analyst.md, rtica-assessor.md (5 total) \u2713\\n  - Other files found: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/references/final-handoff.md, plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md, plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md, plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md, plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md (5 additional files)\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The five named agents do call backlog_view(summary=False), but the claim asks to report other files under plugins/development-harness/ that do so. Five skill files in the work-backlog-item and complete-implementation skills contain backlog_view(summary=False) calls, making the claim incomplete as stated.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T10:37:00.135637Z</sub>\\n\\nCorrects claim 9 of entry 2026-09-19T10:26:10.746520Z\\n\\nCLAIM 9 CORRECTION: Distinguishing narrowed (section=/sections=) vs whole-body (summary=False, no section filter) calls\\n\\nThe previous analysis conflated all files mentioning \\\"backlog_view\\\" and \\\"summary=False\\\". A proper analysis must classify each call:\\n\\n**Five Agent Files \u2014 Call Classification:**\\n\\n| Agent File | Line | Call Type | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| alignment-analyst.md | 31 | Narrowed | `summary=False, sections=[\\\"description\\\", \\\"Impact Radius\\\"]` |\\n| backlog-item-groomer.md | 60 | Whole-body | `summary=False)` to fetch the full item |\\n| backlog-item-groomer.md | 67 | Narrowed | `summary=False, sections=[\\\"Impact Radius\\\"]` |\\n| classifier.md | 26 | Whole-body | `summary=False)` and read the item description |\\n| impact-analyst.md | 28 | Whole-body | `summary=False)` to fetch the full item |\\n| rtica-assessor.md | 42 | Narrowed | `summary=False, sections=[\\\"description\\\", \\\"Impact Radius\\\", \\\"Fact-Check\\\"]` |\\n| rtica-assessor.md | 95 | Narrowed | `sections=[\\\"Impact Radius\\\", \\\"Fact-Check\\\", \\\"Issue Classification\\\"]` |\\n\\n**Summary \u2014 Agents**: 4 narrowed calls (alignment-analyst, backlog-item-groomer line 67, rtica-assessor x2), 3 whole-body calls (backlog-item-groomer line 60, classifier, impact-analyst)\\n\\n**Five Skill Files \u2014 Call Classification:**\\n\\n| Skill File | Line | Call Type | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| groom/error.md | 47 | Narrowed | `section=\\\"Context\\\"` |\\n| complete-implementation/final-handoff.md | 19 | Narrowed | `section=\\\"Concerns\\\"` |\\n| close/start.md | 114 | Narrowed | `sections=[\\\"Acceptance Criteria\\\"]` |\\n| close/start.md | 134 | Whole-body | `summary=False)` (no sections filter) |\\n| groom/swarm.md | 124 | Narrowed | `section='RT-ICA'` |\\n| groom/finalize.md | 143 | Narrowed | `section='{section-name}'` |\\n\\n**Summary \u2014 Skills**: 5 narrowed calls, 1 whole-body call\\n\\n**Updated Verdict**: The original claim is PARTIALLY VALID but INCOMPLETE. The five named agents do call `backlog_view(summary=False)`, but a complete analysis shows: (a) each agent makes strategic choices between whole-body and narrowed reads, and (b) five additional files in skills/ also make these calls, showing a systematic pattern across the codebase, not confined to agents.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:07.292876Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-19T10:50:32.82