\u2026 either (a) \u2026 (b) \u2026 or (c)\\\". AC 4 lists test functions. Both need rework as observable checks.\\n  5. Plan `Pe6bcc5c2` reports 100% complete, but its implementation was never merged (lived only on unpushed local branch `worktree-agent-a07620dae7e4b301c`; PR #3642 re-applies this work).\\n\\nA governing specification that asserts completion when 5 sub-items remain open is a contract violation.\\n\\n**Owner awareness:** Both concerns are known to the owner and represent conscious decisions recorded in the 2026-09-19 comment. The owner approves keeping `map=True` \\\"and record its limit,\\\" acknowledging #3059 (bounding MAP) as required follow-up. The owner has also approved dropping the ARCHITECTURE.md edit from PR #3642 (per observations: \\\"owner has approved dropping that commit\\\"), which mitigates concern 2.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-20T21:33:10.838568Z \u2014 Refining creation-time acceptance criteria into concrete, verifiable checks tied to the artifact's behavioral boundary (the runtime hint strings), per grooming scope.</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] No hint recommends retrieving everything as its first suggestion, per R7\\n- [ ] The over-budget hint offers an action a narrowed caller has not already taken\\n- [ ] Hints name only mechanisms present in the response they accompany\\n- [ ] Addresses appearing in a hint are valid in that same response\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:33:10.838587Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-20T21:51:24.122597Z \u2014 Reconciling AC 2 with the ordinal-compatibility open question discovered during orchestrator pre-planning verification (see RT-ICA reconciliation entry, 2026-08-21) \u2014 the original AC 2 prescribed navigate= unconditionally without confirming sections_index's [N] indices are valid navigate ordinals.</summary>\\n\\n1. Given `backlog_view(selector=<item>, summary=True)` on an i