ed to produce that exact response. It must name the token-bounded pagination mechanism that actually exists in this package (`navigate=<ordinal>`, `head=<tokens>`, `skip_tokens=<offset>`) as the applicable next call for extracting a windowed slice of an oversized section \u2014 matching the pattern already implemented in `disclosure_handler.py`'s `next_call` hint.\\n\\nIn both cases, every parameter name and address named in the hint text must correspond to a mechanism and value actually present in the response object it accompanies (R7's third prohibition) \u2014 e.g. an ordinal named in a hint must appear in that same response's `sections_index`.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T11:19:24.933234Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view(summary=True)` (the default) returns a compact manifest, the `_hint` field's first recommended call must be a narrowing action (`section=`/`sections=`) \u2014 an unqualified full-content load (`summary=False` with no section) must not appear as the first suggestion, and may appear only as a subordinate/fallback option after narrower ones.\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view()` returns an over-budget response (`_over_budget: true`) for a caller who already narrowed to a single section, the `_usage` field must not repeat that same `section=`/`sections=` narrowing. Per the repo owner's 2026-09-19 decision, it names `backlog_view(selector=..., map=True)` as the next call \u2014 and states, in the same hint text, that `map=True` is not guaranteed to stay within the token budget on a large item (MAP is unbounded per `ARCHITECTURE.md:1278-1286`, tracked by open #3059). The hint does not present `map=True` as an unconditionally safe next step.\\n\\nBecause the over-budget response currently carries no field that `map=`, `navigate=`, `head=`, or `skip_tokens=` resolves against, R7's third prohibition (\\\"never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies\\\") remains unmet for this hint even after the `map=True` fix lands. This item's Dependencies and Blockers sections record that gap rather than asserting full compliance \u2014 closing it depends on #3059.\\n\\nThe `backlog_view` tool's `summary` parameter schema description must list a section-scoped read before an unscoped full-content read, matching the `_hint` ordering. `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`'s remaining-ownership/debt table must continue to list `#3060` as open until the criteria above are actually met on `origin/main` \u2014 not merely drafted on an open PR.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:40:04.138071Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-19T13:56:20.977690Z \u2014 Output validation retry 1, 2026-09-19</summary>\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the confirmed change surface is two string-construction functions in one file (`_build_compact_manifest()`'s `_hint`, `_build_over_budget_view()`'s `_usage` in `backlog_core/server.py`). No response schema/field-name changes are anticipated (existing tests pin field/key names, not full hint text), no other package needs modification (`disclosure_handler.py` is reference-only, already R7-compliant), and RT-ICA verdict is READY with 0 MISSING inputs. Validation is bounded to re-running the ~9 identified test files/functions listed in Files and Acceptance Criteria.\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T11:19:24.933302Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-19T13:56:20.977690Z \u2014 Output validation retry 1, 2026-09-19</summary>\\n\\nSmall, unchanged in kind from prior grooming, but now includes landing already-drafted work rather than only writing it: (1) merge PR #3642's `_hint` reorder and `narrowed_to_single_section`/`map=True` branch to `main`, (2) fix the `summary` parameter's `Field(description=...)` ordering (not yet touched by PR #3642), (3) confirm `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`'s debt-table edit either doesn't land or is corrected to keep listing `#3060`, (4) re-run the test files listed in Files/Acceptance Criteria 7. No response schema/field-name changes are need