regex/'`, the exact narrowing action the caller already performed to produce this response, and it never mentions `navigate=`, `head=`, or `skip_tokens=` (verified: `backlog_core/server.py:2379-2387`).\\n3. Compare both strings against `disclosure_handler.py`'s `_handle_extract()` `next_call` hint (`backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:487-490`), which only emits a `skip_tokens=`-based continuation and never recommends an exhausted or absent action \u2014 this is the in-package pattern the two violating hints deviate from.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T11:19:24.933127Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Call `backlog_view(selector='<any item with a non-trivial body>', summary=True)` (the default mode) on origin/main and inspect the returned `_hint` field. Its first line still reads `Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)` \u2014 an unqualified full-content load is recommended before any narrower option (re-verified 2026-09-19: `backlog_core/server.py:2101-2104`; unchanged since 2026-08-21).\\n2. Call `backlog_view(selector='<item>', summary=False, section='<a single section that is itself >4000 tokens>')`. The narrowed request is still over budget. Inspect the returned `_usage` field \u2014 it still recommends `sections=[...]`, `section='0,1,3'`, or `section='/regex/'`, the exact narrowing the caller already performed, and never mentions `map=`, `navigate=`, `head=`, or `skip_tokens=` (re-verified 2026-09-19: `backlog_core/server.py:2176-2184`).\\n3. Both violations above are reproducible against `origin/main` HEAD `a75f11f0a5892979c5d72c316a6d3fe5a1007938` as of 2026-09-19 \u2014 open PR #3642 (branch `fix/3060-backlog-view-r7-hints`) fixes step 1 and partially fixes step 2 (adds a `narrowed_to_single_section` branch naming `map=True`), but that PR is open and unmerged, so neither fix is reproducible against `main` yet.\\n4. Compare both strings against `disclosure_handler.py`'s `_handle_extract()` `next_call` hint (`backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:549-555`), which only emits a `navigate=`/`head=`/`skip_tokens=`-based continuation and never recommends an exhausted or absent action \u2014 the in-package pattern both violating hints still deviate from on `main`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 small change, disproportionate effect on agent behaviour\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:16:26.881207Z</sub>\\n\\n**Root Cause**: Hints in `_build_compact_manifest()` and `_build_over_budget_view()` were written as freeform guidance without reference to the R7 normative requirement or consultation with the disclosure_handler.py reference implementation.\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n- R7 requirement (agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164) is explicit: hints must never recommend full retrieval first, never recommend actions already exhausted, and never name mechanisms absent from the response\\n- _build_compact_manifest (server.py:2306-2309): _hint field leads with \\\"Load full content: summary=False\\\", violating R7 clause \\\"never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\"\\n- _build_over_budget_view (server.py:2379-2387): _usage field recommends section= selection but does not document navigate= + skip_tokens= parameters, violating R7 clause \\\"never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies\\\"\\n- disclosure_handler.py:487-490 demonstrates correct pattern: next_call hint uses navigate=\\\"{ordinal}\\\" (section address) with head={head_tokens} and skip_tokens={next_skip}, all parameters present in BoundedResponse structure being returned\\n- Root-cause mechanism: independent hint construction without consulting R7 requirement or reference implementation left two response-building functions generating incompatible guidance\\n\\n**Fix Scope**:\\n- Rewrite _hint in _build_compact_manifest to recommend section selection first (using section= or sections= parameters) and defer full-content retrieval to an alternative, not a primary action\\n- Rewrite _usage in _build_over_budget_view to name navigate=, head=, and skip_tokens= parameters as primary pagination mechanism, matching the sections_index discovery already included in the response\\n- Ensure both hints reference only mechanisms and addresses present in the response object they accompany (R7 requirement)\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T10:04:10.796556Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: Direct source verification (2026-09-19) against R7 requirement and reference implementation\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n\\n1. **Observed failure**: Agent receives `backlog_view()` response hints that violate R7 (agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164), steering navigation away from paginated parameters (navigate=, head=, skip_tokens=)\\n\\n2. **Why (proximate cause)**: Two hint-building functions generate text without consulting R7 requirement or reference implementation\\n   - `_build_compact_manifest()` (server.py:2101-2104): `_hint` field is hardcoded to lead with `summary=False` (full-content)\\n   - `_build_over_budget_view()` (server.py:2147-2189): `_usage` field built unconditionally without parameter access to detect caller's prior narrowing\\n\\n3. **Why (architecture gap)**: `_build_over_budget_view()` function signature (line 2147: `_build_over_budget_view(result, full_chars, selector)`) receives no parameter carrying \\\"caller already narrowed\\\" state. Callsite at server.py line 2143 passes only the result object, full char count, and selector. No request-context parameter available for the function to branch on.\\n\\n4. **Why (design decision)**: Both functions built independently as response formatters without cross-reference to disclosure_handler.py (line 487-490), which already implements the correct pattern: `next_call` hint uses navigate=, head=, skip_tokens= parameters all present in the BoundedResponse being returned.\\n\\n5. **Root cause**: Hint-generation functions were authored without reading the R7 normative requirement (agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md) or consulting disclosure_handler.py's reference implementation. The functions' signatures and callsites (no narrowing-state parameter) encode an early design decision that hints are response-formatters with no request context, separating them from the infrastructure (disclosure_handler.py) that already solved pagination-hint generation correctly.\\n\\n**Fix locus**: Multiple sites require changes:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2101-2104`: Reorder `_hint` to name section-narrowing first\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2147-2189`: Add `narrowed_to_single_section: bool` parameter to detect caller's prior narrowing; branch `_usage` to offer map=True instead of section-narrowing when already narrowed (PR #3642 partial implementation)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (callsite 2143): Pass narrowing-detection flag from request context to _build_over_budget_view\\n- Post-#3059 (MAP pagination): Update map=True hint to name navigate=, head=, skip_tokens= once MAP response fields are bounded and present\\n\\n**Interim constraint** (owner decision, 2026-09-19): Keep map=True as narrowed over-budget hint. Safety ceiling: MAP has no size bound until #3059 ships.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-19T10:34:01.545951Z</sub>\\n\\nSupersedes entry 2026-09-19T10:04:10.796556Z (2026-09-19), which cites wrong disclosure_handler.py line and incorrect callsite.\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys root-cause analysis via direct source verification (2026-09-19, origin/main a75f11f0a)\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n\\n1. **Observed failure**: `backlog_view()` response hints violate all three R7 prohibitions (agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:158-163), steering navigation away from pagination mechanisms\\n\\n2. **Why (proximate cause)**: Two hint-building functions generate text without consulting R7 requirement or reference implementation\\n   - `_build_compact_manifest()` (server.py:2101-2104): `_hint` hardcoded to lead with summary=False\\n   - `_build_over_budget_view()` (server.py:2176-2184): `_usage` built unconditionally, no branching\\n\\n3. **Why (architecture gap)**: `_build_over_budget_view()` signature (line 2147) receives no parameter carrying \\\"caller already narrowed\\\" state. Callsite at server.py:2513 passes only result, full_chars, selector \u2014 no request context available for branching.\\n\\n4. **Why (design decision)**: Both functions built independently as response formatters with no cross-reference to disclosure_handler.py:549-555, which already implements correct pattern. The `next_call` field demonstrates R7-compliant format: `navigate=\\\"{ordinal}\\\", head={head_tokens}, skip_tokens={next_skip}` \u2014 all parameters present in BoundedResponse being returned.\\n\\n5. **Root cause**: Hints authored without reading R7 normative requirement (agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:158-163) or consulting disclosure_handler.py's reference implementation. Function signatures and callsites encode early design decision: hints are response-formatters with no request context, separating them from pagination infrastructure (disclosure_handler.py) that already solved this correctly.\\n\\n**Fix Locus on origin/main**:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2101-2104`: Reorder `_hint` to recommend section-narrowing first (section= or sections=), defer full-content to secondary\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2176-2184`: Rewrite `_usage` to name pagination parameters (navigate=, head=, skip_tokens=) matching disclosure_handler.py:549-555 pattern\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2513` callsite: Pass narrowing-detection flag to _build_over_budget_view to enable branching when caller narrowed\\n- After #3059 (MAP pagination) ships: Ensure map=True hint includes navigate=, head=, skip_tokens= in response\\n\\n**State of PR #3642** (separate): Addresses reordering _hint and detecting narrowed state (partial fix). Leaves unmet: response has no navigate=/head=/skip_tokens= fields to reference in map=True hint (R7 prohibition 3), and map=True hint itself can over-budget until MAP is paginated (#3059).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"982d994a9795a4078230d0998b5828d3d920e074b383b8159cc440c60de0b59e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVkxQdQ\"}"}